              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When you're running a trucking business, every piece of equipment has a long-term cost attached to it. For many owner-operators and fleet managers, understanding dry van trailer maintenance costs is just as important as knowing the purchase price. A trailer might look like a simple piece of equipment, but over the years, it requires consistent upkeep to stay safe, compliant, and reliable on the road.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "From brakes and tires to flooring and doors, knowing the maintenance costs for a trailer helps you plan your budget, avoid costly breakdowns, and extend the life of your equipment. At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, we know most operators are focused on one simple goal: keep freight moving and keep operating costs predictable.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-why-matters",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Dry Van Trailer Maintenance Costs Matter",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "why-matters"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-matters-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Many trucking businesses focus heavily on truck maintenance, but trailers often get less attention until something breaks. The reality is that a well-maintained dry van trailer can stay productive for many years, while neglected equipment quickly becomes a financial burden.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-matters-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>Routine maintenance helps operators:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
