                {
                  "id": "h-reduce-costs",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "How to Reduce Dry Van Trailer Maintenance Costs",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "reduce-costs"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-reduce-costs-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "While every trailer will require upkeep, there are smart ways operators can reduce long-term costs.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-reduce-costs-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "num",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "points": [],
                        "num": "1",
                        "title": "Invest in Quality Equipment",
                        "intro": "Higher-quality trailers are built with materials designed for durability and long service life: reinforced flooring, corrosion-resistant components, durable sidewalls, and high-quality suspension."
                      },
                      {
                        "points": [],
                        "num": "2",
                        "title": "Follow Preventive Maintenance Schedules",
                        "intro": "Regular inspections should include tire pressure and wear checks, brake system inspections, structural integrity checks, and lighting and electrical testing. Catching small issues early prevents expensive repairs later."
                      },
                      {
                        "points": [],
                        "num": "3",
                        "title": "Train Drivers to Spot Issues Early",
                        "intro": "Drivers spend the most time around the equipment. Encouraging drivers to report uneven tire wear, door problems, unusual noises, or suspension concerns can resolve problems before they become major repairs."
                      },
                      {
                        "points": [],
                        "num": "4",
                        "title": "Protect Trailers During Loading",
                        "intro": "Many maintenance issues start during loading operations. Proper loading procedures help prevent forklift damage to the flooring, sidewall impacts, and door hinge stress."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-long-term-value",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The Long-Term Value of Reliable Dry Vans",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "long-term-value"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-long-term-value-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A well-maintained dry van trailer is one of the most versatile and cost-effective pieces of equipment in the trucking industry.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-long-term-value-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>Dry vans remain the most commonly used trailer type because they:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-long-term-value-3",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Protect cargo from the weather"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Handle a wide range of freight"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Offer strong payload capacity"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Maintain resale value when properly maintained"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-long-term-value-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For many trucking companies, a dependable trailer becomes a long-term asset that supports consistent revenue for years. That's why operators often look closely at both initial purchase price and long-term maintenance costs when comparing trailer options.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
